'''''Stranvaesia nussia''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Rosaceae]]. It is an [[evergreen]] tree<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://treesandshrubsonline.org/articles/stranvaesia/stranvaesia-nussia/|title=Stranvaesia nussia - Trees and Shrubs Online|website=treesandshrubsonline.org|access-date=2020-01-29}}</ref> which ranges from [[Nepal]] and Tibet to south-central China ([[Yunnan]]), Indochina (Laos, Myanmar, and Thailand), and the Philippines.<ref name = powo/>

== Description ==
* Height: 5-9m tall.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=200011829|title=Stranvaesia nussia in Flora of China @ efloras.org|website=www.efloras.org|access-date=2020-01-29}}</ref>
* Branches: pilose when young, purple/brown when old.<ref name=":1" />
* Petiole: 1&nbsp;cm.<ref name=":1" />

== Habitat ==
''S. nussia'' are restricted to particular elevational ranges in the Himalayas, along with being a rare tree species found in the [[Binsar Wildlife Sanctuary]].<ref>{{Cite journal|last1=Majila|first1=Bhagwan|last2=Kala|first2=Chandra|date=April 12, 2009|title=Forest Structure and Regeneration along the Altitudinal Gradient in the Binsar Wildlife Sanctuary, Uttarakhand Himalaya, India|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225482495|journal=Russian Journal of Ecology|volume=41|pages=75–83|via=ResearchGate|doi=10.1134/s1067413610010157|s2cid=22272774}}</ref>

